# If you prefer the allow list template instead of the deny list, see community template:
# https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/community/Golang/Go.AllowList.gitignore
#
# Binaries for programs and plugins
*.exe
*.exe~
*.dll
*.so
*.dylib

# Test binary, built with `go test -c`
*.test

# Code coverage profiles and other test artifacts
*.out
coverage.*
*.coverprofile
profile.cov

# Dependency directories (remove the comment below to include it)
# vendor/

# Go workspace file
go.work
go.work.sum

# Runtime config carries real credentials (DB password, RAGFlow API key).
# Secrets must be injected via RGX_* environment variables, never committed.
config/config.yaml
config/config.local.yaml

# Local secrets and environment files
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
.env.local
*.secret

# Runtime data and databases
data/
*.db
*.db-journal
*.db-wal
*.db-shm

# Encrypted runtime secrets and keys created by the first-run wizard
config/runtime.secrets.json
config/.master.key
config/rsa_setup.pem

# Logs
logs/
*.log

# Build artifacts
web/dist/

# Staged frontend build for go:embed (copied from web/dist by the release
# pipeline / release-drill before `go build -tags=webfs_embed`).
internal/webfs/dist/
web/dist2/
web/dist3/
web/web.rar
web/node_modules/
web/coverage/
web/coverage-report/
web/test-results/
web/playwright-report/
.gocache/
bin/
test-results/
ragflow-x-server
dist-drill/
.go-test-service.json
run/

# IDE / OS
.idea/
.vscode/

# Local scratch dirs (kept out of VCS pending per-file review)
tmp/

# tasks/ is a transient execution area (see tasks/README.md): it is emptied at
# the end of every slice, so its contents never belong in history.
/tasks/

# Development docs and local test data: intentionally untracked until each
# file is reviewed for release (see doc/126 pre-release review report).
# Do NOT add these back in bulk; whitelist individual files after review.
#
# Policy (2026-11-28, user decision — it supersedes the 2026-11-27 attempt
# recorded in doc/321, which had put doc/develop/ under version control):
#
#   the implementation archive stays local.
#
# doc/develop/ is a developer's decision + evidence record, written on one
# machine, citing that machine, and edited while the work moves. It is not a
# deliverable. What ships with the code is the long-lived contracts
# (doc/specification/) and the user manual (doc/user/) — the two things a
# reader of the repository is expected to act on.
#
# Tracked:      doc/specification/**/*.md, doc/specification/api/api-reference.{md,html},
#               doc/user/**                    (manual; README links into it)
# Stay local:   doc/develop/ (decision + evidence records),
#               doc/operations/ (runbooks; quoting real hosts and tokens),
#               doc/environment/ (machine-specific; carries the real .env values),
#               drafts, TODO.txt, rendered .docx/.pdf, performance captures.
#
# Consequence, stated so it is not discovered later: a gate that compares code
# against an engineering record (`s19.docs-ledger`, the doc-anchor gate) has
# nothing to read on a clone. Those rows answer "this tree cannot answer"
# (exit 3 / SKIP) there and still run on the author's tree — the same boundary
# `doc/operations/` already lives behind. See scripts/release-gate/docs-ledger.sh.
#
# Credential discipline still applies to every tracked document: the pre-commit
# secret-scan covers docs exactly as it covers code (doc/321 §3 lists file +
# category, never the value).
/doc/*
# `/test/*` (not `/test/`) so the reusable regression harness below can be
# re-included: an excluded directory cannot have tracked children.
/test/*
# Exception (v0.6.1): the scenario-template end-to-end harness is part of the
# delivery — it is how "download it and it works" is proven before a release.
# The corpora it consumes (test/*-docs) stay local-only.
!/test/e2e/
# Run state and pycache are per-machine; the evidence file is the deliverable.
/test/e2e/**/out/state-*.json
__pycache__/
# Exception (v0.5.0): the user-facing documentation set under doc/user/ is part
# of the release (README links into it) and is tracked. Everything else under
# doc/ (develop/, blog/, performance/, VIDEOS) stays local-only.
!/doc/user/
# Exception to the exception (2026-11-26): the *rendered* deliverables under doc/user/
# are not repository content. They are Word/PDF builds of the markdown beside them,
# generated locally (tmp/build-*-guide.py), and their screenshots carry the internal
# test deployment's address — an address that must not travel with the repository, and
# that makes every one of them stale the moment a route or a menu label changes. The markdown is the source of truth and stays tracked; the binaries are
# release/delivery artifacts. `git add -A` will no longer pick them up.
/doc/user/**/*.docx
/doc/user/**/*.pdf
# Exception (v0.6.6): the generated API reference under doc/specification/api/ is a
# deliverable — it is what gets sent to integrators — so it is tracked, and its freshness
# is a gate row (s28.api-doc: regenerate, compare byte-for-byte, refuse an ignored product).
# Since 2026-11-27 (doc/321) the whole specification set is tracked, not just those two
# files: the norms are what the code is reviewed against, so they belong in the diff.
!/doc/specification/
/doc/specification/*
!/doc/specification/**/*.md
!/doc/specification/api/
/doc/specification/api/*
!/doc/specification/api/api-reference.md
!/doc/specification/api/api-reference.html
# The implementation archive is local (2026-11-28 policy above): decision records,
# evidence, diagrams and scratch notes under doc/develop/ are all out of the index.
/doc/develop/
# Rendered binaries are build artifacts, never repository content (doc/321).
/doc/**/*.docx
/doc/**/*.pdf
# Demo videos are large binaries hosted as release assets, not repository
# content; the markdown guides reference ./images/ only.
/doc/user/videos/

# Local build artifacts that keep landing in the repo root
/ragflow-x
/ragflow-x-server
/deploy-drill
/difydsl
/perf-baseline
/perf-cleanup
# Linux server binaries produced by release drills (M216: 64.94 MB binary
# was accidentally committed in M213; untracked and ignored from now on).
/build/
/testcontract-pg
/go-coverage
/go-coverage-*
/go-coverage.*
/go-testquality.test
*.test

# Local integration runtime and scratch artifacts
/.service-test*
/blog/.tmp-*
/blog/.tmp_*
/blog/tmp-*
/docs.zip
/sync-*.png
/tmp-query/

# Local-only agent red lines (never commit)
/AGENTS.local.md

# Reusable local-only tooling (never commit; mirrors doc/ and AGENTS.local.md)
/localenv/

# Local drill/private config carries real credentials (drill rc3 engine on the
# internal test host + dedicated postgres/redis, custom ports); never commit.
# Mirrors config/config.yaml.
config/config.drill*.yaml

# First-run wizard key/secrets backups (master key + encrypted secrets), never commit
config/.master.key.*
config/runtime.secrets.json.*
